{"key1": "DA", "subcard": "_d_a~~h0_45_upa", "iast": "upadhā", "h": "upadhā", "sense_tag": "7", "ru": "<div n=\"1\">— 7) {#upahita#} вероятно {%подосланный к кому-л. в качестве шпиона%} (<ab>vgl.</ab> {#praRi): vyaktaM tvamapyupahitaH pARqavEH pApadeSaja#}\n<ls>MBH. 8,1861.</ls> <ls n=\"MBH.\">12,4159.</ls> <ls n=\"MBH. 12,\">4161.</ls> <ls>BENFEY</ls> (<ls>PAÑCAT. Bd. I, S. 581</ls>) переводит это слово во втором месте как {%те%},\n[Page3-0915]\n{%на кого враги устроили засаду%}, в третьем — как {%притворившийся.%}", "de": "<div n=\"1\">— 7) {#upahita#} wohl {%als Spion zu Jmd geschickt%} (<ab>vgl.</ab> {#praRi): vyaktaM tvamapyupahitaH pARqavEH pApadeSaja#}\n<ls>MBH. 8,1861.</ls> <ls n=\"MBH.\">12,4159.</ls> <ls n=\"MBH. 12,\">4161.</ls> <ls>BENFEY</ls> (<ls>PAÑCAT. Bd. I, S. 581</ls>) übersetzt das Wort an der zweiten Stelle durch {%diejenigen%}\n[Page3-0915]\n{%denen ihre Feinde nachgestellt haben%}, an der dritten durch {%verstellt.%}", "equivalence_type": "explanatory", "source_type": "attested", "stratum": "", "differentia": "", "review_status": "ai_translated", "reviewer": null, "provenance": {"model": "sonnet", "generator": "gen_opt_harness2.batched-masked", "schema_version": "pwg_ru.workflow_meta.v1", "root": "DA", "safe_root": "_d_a", "rootmap_sha256": "29ac182af41e4be8254a0a137fc08a355153b793cba4e1fdd80ef35b423f90fd", "input_raw_sha256": "950297575a19359b52e121f6d71767d11659a6846eee7e7cf0781fe69dbf93e7", "input_portrait_sha256": "88fff0abcdff5d54bba899881304b5aea8c545026358f71d04379fa3848ad4f4", "generated_at": "2026-06-29T12:31:01Z", "wf_file": "wf_output_da_a.json", "promoted_by": "promote_final_cards.py"}, "dcs_freq": {"band": 4, "count": 975, "hapax": false, "attested": true, "core80": true, "matched": "compound", "matched_key": "upadhā", "pos": {"counts": {"NOUN": 98, "VERB": 877}, "shares": {"NOUN": 0.1005, "VERB": 0.8995}, "band": {"NOUN": 5, "VERB": 5}, "dominant": "VERB", "dominant_share": 0.8995, "total": 975}, "genre": {"counts": {"sastra": 78, "kosa": 1, "smrti": 9, "epic": 51, "bhasya": 9, "purana": 4, "katha": 5, "vyakarana": 42, "tantra": 2, "sutra": 204, "kavya": 3, "bauddha": 1, "brahmana": 148, "atharva": 1, "yajus": 412}, "band": {"sastra": 5, "kosa": 3, "smrti": 5, "epic": 5, "bhasya": 5, "purana": 4, "katha": 4, "vyakarana": 5, "tantra": 3, "sutra": 5, "kavya": 4, "bauddha": 2, "brahmana": 5, "atharva": 3, "yajus": 5}}, "era": {"counts": {"Classical": 90, "Epic-Purana": 64, "Sutra-Sastra": 255, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 148, "Vedic": 413}, "band": {"Classical": 5, "Epic-Purana": 5, "Sutra-Sastra": 5, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 5, "Vedic": 5}}}, "en": "<div n=\"1\">— 7) {#upahita#} probably sent as a spy to someone (<ab>vgl.</ab> {#praRi): vyaktaM tvamapyupahitaH pARqavEH pApadeSaja#}\n<ls>MBH. 8,1861.</ls> <ls n=\"MBH.\">12,4159.</ls> <ls n=\"MBH. 12,\">4161.</ls> <ls>BENFEY</ls> (<ls>PAÑCAT. Bd. I, S. 581</ls>) translates the word in the second passage as those against whom their enemies have laid snares, and in the third passage as dissembling."}
