ajus": 5}}, "era": {"counts": {"Vedic": 143, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 208, "Sutra-Sastra": 692, "Classical": 299, "Epic-Purana": 218}, "band": {"Vedic": 5, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 5, "Sutra-Sastra": 5, "Classical": 5, "Epic-Purana": 5}}}, "en": "<div n=\"p\">— {#ni#}\n<div n=\"1\"> 1) to set down, to lay down, to place, to put in or on; to install: {#u\\rvyAH pa\\do ni da^DAti\\ sAnO^#}\n<ls>ṚV. 1,146,2.</ls> {#(agniH) ni yaM da\\Durma^nu\\zyA^su vi\\kzu#}\n<ls n=\"ṚV. 1,\">148,1.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV.\">4,2,1.</ls> {#ni tvA^ daDe\\ vara\\ A pf^Ti\\vyAH#}\n<ls n=\"ṚV.\">3,23,4.</ls> {#ma\\nu\\zvattvA\\ ni DI^mahi#}\n<ls n=\"ṚV.\">5,21,1.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV.\">6,15,15.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV.\">8,19,17.</ls> <ls>VS. 15,49.</ls> <ls>ŚAT. BR. 2,2,2,13.</ls> {#ni da^De\\ hasta^yo\\rvajra^m#}\n<ls>ṚV. 1,81,4.</ls> {#a\\yaM vA^M BA\\go nihi^taH#}\n<ls n=\"ṚV. 1,\">183,4.</ls> {#aBi^nne Ki\\lye ni da^DAti deva\\yum#}\n<ls n=\"ṚV.\">6,28,2.</ls> {#i\\zwasya\\ maDye\\ adi^ti\\rni DA^tu naH#}\n<ls n=\"ṚV.\">10,11,2.</ls> {#u\\raU lo\\ke ni DI^yasva#} rest in the vast space\n<ls>AV. 18,2,20.</ls> {#vaha^ pi\\tfByo\\ yatrE^nA\\nvetTa\\ nihi^tAnparA\\ke#}\n<ls>VS. 35,20.</ls> {#ni te\\ mano\\ mana^si DAyya\\sme#} may thy mind merge into my mind\n<ls>ṚV. 10,10,3.</ls> — <ls>ŚAT. BR. 1,7,1,12.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 1,\">8,1,13.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">5,2,3,5.</ls> {#(yatrAsya puruzasya mftasya) apsu lohitaM ca retaSca niDIyate#} to pass over into, to be absorbed into\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">14,6,2,13.</ls> {#udIcInAnasya pAdo niDattAt#}\n<ls>AIT. BR. 2,6.</ls>\n<ls>KĀTY. ŚR. 2,2,19.</ls> <ls n=\"KĀTY. ŚR. 2,\">3,1.</ls> {#kftAdi#}\n<ls n=\"KĀTY. ŚR.\">15,7,18.</ls> {#aSvasya SiSnaM mahizyupasTe niDatte#} lays in her lap\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 13,5,2,2.</ls> {#uraHsu pARIn#}\n<ls>LĀṬY. 2,11,20.</ls> {#tasmE tfRaM nidaDO#} he laid a blade of grass before him\n<ls>KENOP 19.</ls> {#aniDAyEva taddravyam#}\n<ls>M. 5,143.</ls>\n<ls>R. 3,60,21.</ls> {#mfgaM BUmO niDAya#}\n<ls>HIT. 34,20.</ls> {#mA niDAH padaM padavyAM sagarasya saMtateH#}\n<ls>RAGH. 3,50.</ls> <ls n=\"RAGH. 3,\">62.</ls> <ls n=\"RAGH.\">12,52.</ls>\n<ls>ŚIŚ. 1,13.</ls> {#Sirasi nidaDAno 'Yjalipuwam#}\n<ls>BHARTṚ. 3,87.</ls>\n<ls>ŚĀK. 105,17.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚĀK.\">69.</ls>\n<ls>PAÑCAT. I,224.</ls> <ls>MEGH. 91.</ls> <ls>AK. 3,3,35.</ls> <ls>BHĀG. P. 1,18,30.</ls> <ls n=\"BHĀG. P.\">3,28,23.</ls> <ls>DHŪRTAS. 92,5.</ls> <ls>BHAṬṬ. 3,35.</ls> {#karO niDAya SirasA#}\n<ls>R. 2,50,21.</ls> {#parezAM nihitaM balam#} laid, deposited\n<ls n=\"R.\">5,73,21.</ls> {#AtmA guhAyAM nihito 'sya jantoH#}\n<ls>ŚVETĀŚV. UP. 3,20.</ls>\n<ls>TAITT. UP. 2,1.</ls> <ls>KAṬHOP. 1,14.</ls> {#UnadvivArzikaM pretaM nidaDyurbAnDavA bahiH . alaMkftya SucO BUmO#} to lay in, thus <ab>v. a.</ab> to bury in\n<ls>M. 5,68.</ls>\n<ls>R. 3,8,20.</ls> {#sa enAM tata AdAya nyaDAdOdaYcanodake#}\n<ls>BHĀG. P. 8,24,19.</ls> {#KadirakIlakena maDyanihitena#}\n<ls>PAÑCAT. 10,7.</ls> <ls n=\"PAÑCAT. 10,\">11.</ls> <ls n=\"PAÑCAT.\">34,21.</ls>\n<ls>HIT. I,168.</ls> {#Gawe nidaDe — aNgulIyakam#}\n<ls>VID. 293.</ls> {#tatra saMDimaternyaDuH#}\n<ls>RĀJA-TAR. 2,105.</ls> {#yasyAmAjyaM niDIyate#}\n<ls>H. 829.</ls> {#GftaniDAyaM#} (<ab>absol.</ab>) {#nihitaH = Gftamiva nihitaH#}\n<ls>P. 3,4,45</ls>, <ab>Schol.</ab> {#SaNKanihitAtpayasaH#}\n<ls>ŚIŚ. 9,46.</ls> {#vAgdaRqo 'Ta manodaRqaH kAyadaRqastaTEva ca .. yasyEte nihitA budDO#}\n<ls>M. 12,10.</ls> {#nihitArTa#}\n<ls>ŚVETĀŚV. UP. 4,1.</ls> With {#antarH ni jA^hu\\zaM Si^Ti\\re DA^tama\\ntaH#}\n<ls>ṚV. 7,71,5.</ls> {#ti\\sro dyAvo\\ nihi^tA antara^smin#}\n<ls n=\"ṚV. 7,\">87,5.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV.\">1,24,7.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV.\">3,55,15.</ls> <ls>AV. 1,13,3.</ls> <ls>H. 1003.</ls> {#(gajacarma) tajjalOGena nItvA ca samudrAntarnyaDIyata#}\n<ls>KATHĀS. 12,112.</ls> {#nihitanayanA#} whose eyes are directed upon (<ab>loc.</ab>)\n<ls>MEGH. 96</ls>, <ab>v. l.</ab> {#nidaDe pratikArecCAmiva Kaqge dfSaM muhuH#}\n<ls>KATHĀS. 10,67.</ls> {#sargAya nidaDe manaH#} to direct one's thoughts upon, to resolve\n<ls>HARIV. 534.</ls> {#iti manasi niDAya#} thus <ab>v. a.</ab> thinking thus within oneself\n<ls>HIT. 87,13.</ls> {#kriyAm#} to apply effort to something: {#nAdravye nihitA kAcitkriyA PalavatI Bavet#}\n<ls>HIT. Pr. 43.</ls> {#karmaRi#} to appoint someone to something: {#pfTagjanocite karmaRyarhato nidaDAti yaH#}\n<ls>RĀJA-TAR. 3,212.</ls>"}
