{"key1": "DA", "subcard": "_d_a~~h0_53_a_bini", "iast": "abhinidhā", "h": "abhinidhā", "sense_tag": "2", "ru": "<div n=\"1\">— 2) {%касаться, приближаться%}: {#kzureRABinidaDAti#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 3,1,2,7.</ls> {#asinA#}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,\">8,2,12.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,8,2,\">13.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,\">4,1,22.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">1,3,4,12.</ls> {#dakziRaM karRamaBiniDAya vAgvAgiti triH#} (уста) {%поднося близко к уху%} (ребёнка)\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">14,9,4,25.</ls> {#mUrDannaBiniDAyASrAvayati#}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">4,4,3,9.</ls> <ls>KĀTY. ŚR. 2,8,2.</ls> <ls n=\"KĀTY. ŚR.\">6,6,9.</ls> <ls>GOBH. 2,9,11.</ls> <ls>KAUŚ. 53. 86.</ls> <ab>partic.</ab> {#aBinihita#} {%прикасающийся%}: {#aBinihita eva savyena pARinA Bavati#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 1,3,4,12.</ls> {#anaBinihito vE puruzo 'nnena ca prARena ca#} {%не соприкасающийся с%}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">7,4,2,9.</ls> {%приближающийся, соприкасающийся%} — так называется <is>Saṃdhi</is>, {%который возникает при слиянии начального%} {#a#} {%с предшествующим%} {#e, o#}, {%и тон, лежащий на таком слоге%} (<ab>urspr.</ab> — вероятно, произносимом дифтонгически как ea, oa),\n<ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 2,13.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT.\">3,7.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 3,\">10.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 3,\">19.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT.\">13,10.</ls>\n<ls>VS. PRĀT. 1,114.</ls> <ls n=\"VS. PRĀT. 1,\">125.</ls>\n<ls>AV. PRĀT. 3,54.</ls>\n<ls>TAITT. PRĀT. 2,8.</ls>\n<ls>ŚĀṄKH. ŚR. 12,13,5</ls> в <ls>Ind. St. 4,230.</ls> Данное под {#aBiniDAna#}\n<ls n=\"Ind. St.\">2.</ls> объяснение следует исправить: {%сближение%} (звуков в произношении, в отличие от непосредственного соединения, {#saMyoga)#}.{# ete ca dvEpadA yaTAgfhItamaBiniDIyante#} {%подчиняются так называемому%} <is>abhinihita</is> <is>Saṃdhi</is>\n<ab>Schol.</ab> к <ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 2,19.</ls> <ab>Schol.</ab> к <ls>VS. PRĀT. 4,61</ls> в <ls>Ind. St. 4,230.</ls> О <is>Sparśa</is> говорится\n<ls>CHĀND. UP. 2,22,5</ls>; {#leSenABanihitA#} (читай с <ab>Schol.</ab> {#leSenAnaBi˚) vaktavyAH#}; <ab>vgl.</ab> к тому же {#aBiniDAna#}\n<ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 6,5.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">9.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">11.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">12.</ls>", "de": "<div n=\"1\">— 2) {%berühren, nahe kommen%}: {#kzureRABinidaDAti#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 3,1,2,7.</ls> {#asinA#}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,\">8,2,12.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,8,2,\">13.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,\">4,1,22.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">1,3,4,12.</ls> {#dakziRaM karRamaBiniDAya vAgvAgiti triH#} (den Mund) {%nahe an das Ohr%} (des Kindes) {%bringend%}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">14,9,4,25.</ls> {#mUrDannaBiniDAyASrAvayati#}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">4,4,3,9.</ls> <ls>KĀTY. ŚR. 2,8,2.</ls> <ls n=\"KĀTY. ŚR.\">6,6,9.</ls> <ls>GOBH. 2,9,11.</ls> <ls>KAUŚ. 53. 86.</ls> <ab>partic.</ab> {#aBinihita#} {%berührt%}: {#aBinihita eva savyena pARinA Bavati#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 1,3,4,12.</ls> {#anaBinihito vE puruzo 'nnena ca prARena ca#} {%sich nicht berührend mit%}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">7,4,2,9.</ls> {%der nahegerückte, berührende%} heisst der <is>Saṃdhi</is>, {%welcher eintritt bei der Verschmelzung eines anlautenden%} {#a#} {%mit einem vorangehenden%} {#e, o#}, {%und der auf einer solchen Silbe%} (<ab>urspr.</ab> wohl diphthongisch ea, oa gesprochen) {%ruhende Ton%},\n<ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 2,13.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT.\">3,7.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 3,\">10.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 3,\">19.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT.\">13,10.</ls>\n<ls>VS. PRĀT. 1,114.</ls> <ls n=\"VS. PRĀT. 1,\">125.</ls>\n<ls>AV. PRĀT. 3,54.</ls>\n<ls>TAITT. PRĀT. 2,8.</ls>\n<ls>ŚĀṄKH. ŚR. 12,13,5</ls> in <ls>Ind. St. 4,230.</ls> Die unter {#aBiniDAna#}\n<ls n=\"Ind. St.\">2.</ls> gegebene Erklärung ist zu verbessern: {%Annäherung%} (der Laute in der Aussprache, im Unterschied von unmittelbarer Verbindung, {#saMyoga)#}.{# ete ca dvEpadA yaTAgfhItamaBiniDIyante#} {%unterliegen dem%} <is>abhinihita</is> {%genannten%} <is>Saṃdhi</is>\n<ab>Schol.</ab> zu <ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 2,19.</ls> <ab>Schol.</ab> zu <ls>VS. PRĀT. 4,61</ls> in <ls>Ind. St. 4,230.</ls> Von den <is>Sparśa</is> heisst es\n<ls>CHĀND. UP. 2,22,5</ls>; {#leSenABanihitA#} (lies mit dem\n<ab>Schol.</ab> {#leSenAnaBi˚) vaktavyAH#}; <ab>vgl.</ab> dazu {#aBiniDAna#}\n<ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 6,5.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">9.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">11.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">12.</ls>", "equivalence_type": "equivalent", "source_type": "attested", "stratum": "", "differentia": "Прямое значение касания/приближения; граммат. применение термина к фонетическому сближению звуков (abhinidhāna как техн. термин).", "review_status": "ai_translated", "reviewer": null, "provenance": {"model": "sonnet", "generator": "gen_opt_harness2.batched-masked", "schema_version": "pwg_ru.workflow_meta.v1", "root": "DA", "safe_root": "_d_a", "rootmap_sha256": "29ac182af41e4be8254a0a137fc08a355153b793cba4e1fdd80ef35b423f90fd", "input_raw_sha256": "28d526b481ed5bb1ef58576cfaec70ca4ada66050408711d73bb056c8a04a7b5", "input_portrait_sha256": "21bb5b6044f7a7f1aca47dfdafaa8a521a0a6d0abacecf1c03dc6d15fdbab80f", "generated_at": "2026-06-29T12:31:01Z", "wf_file": "wf_output_da_a.json", "promoted_by": "promote_final_cards.py"}, "dcs_freq": {"band": 3, "count": 59, "hapax": false, "attested": true, "core80": false, "matched": "compound", "matched_key": "abhinidhā", "pos": {"counts": {"VERB": 59}, "shares": {"VERB": 1.0}, "band": {"VERB": 5}, "dominant": "VERB", "dominant_share": 1.0, "total": 59}, "genre": {"counts": {"sutra": 26, "brahmana": 32, "upanisad": 1}, "band": {"sutra": 5, "brahmana": 5, "upanisad": 2}}, "era": {"counts": {"Sutra-Sastra": 26, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 33}, "band": {"Sutra-Sastra": 5, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 5}}}, "en": "<div n=\"1\">— 2) to touch, to approach closely: {#kzureRABinidaDAti#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 3,1,2,7.</ls> {#asinA#}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,\">8,2,12.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,8,2,\">13.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,\">4,1,22.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">1,3,4,12.</ls> {#dakziRaM karRamaBiniDAya vAgvAgiti triH#} bringing (the mouth) close to the ear (of the child)\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">14,9,4,25.</ls> {#mUrDannaBiniDAyASrAvayati#}\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">4,4,3,9.</ls> <ls>KĀTY. ŚR. 2,8,2.</ls> <ls n=\"KĀTY. ŚR.\">6,6,9.</ls> <ls>GOBH. 2,9,11.</ls> <ls>KAUŚ. 53. 86.</ls> <ab>partic.</ab> {#aBinihita#} touched: {#aBinihita eva savyena pARinA Bavati#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 1,3,4,12.</ls> {#anaBinihito vE puruzo 'nnena ca prARena ca#} not touching, not coming into contact with\n<ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">7,4,2,9.</ls> the term for that which has drawn near, that which is touching is <is>Saṃdhi</is>, which occurs in the fusion of an initial {#a#} with a preceding {#e, o#}, and the tone resting upon such a syllable (<ab>urspr.</ab> probably pronounced diphthongally as ea, oa),\n<ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 2,13.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT.\">3,7.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 3,\">10.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 3,\">19.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT.\">13,10.</ls>\n<ls>VS. PRĀT. 1,114.</ls> <ls n=\"VS. PRĀT. 1,\">125.</ls>\n<ls>AV. PRĀT. 3,54.</ls>\n<ls>TAITT. PRĀT. 2,8.</ls>\n<ls>ŚĀṄKH. ŚR. 12,13,5</ls> in <ls>Ind. St. 4,230.</ls> The explanation given under {#aBiniDAna#}\n<ls n=\"Ind. St.\">2.</ls> is to be corrected: approach (of sounds in pronunciation, as distinct from immediate conjunction, {#saMyoga)#}.{# ete ca dvEpadA yaTAgfhItamaBiniDIyante#} are subject to the <is>abhinihita</is> called <is>Saṃdhi</is>\n<ab>Schol.</ab> to <ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 2,19.</ls> <ab>Schol.</ab> to <ls>VS. PRĀT. 4,61</ls> in <ls>Ind. St. 4,230.</ls> Of the <is>Sparśa</is> it is said\n<ls>CHĀND. UP. 2,22,5</ls>; {#leSenABanihitA#} (read with\n<ab>Schol.</ab> {#leSenAnaBi˚) vaktavyAH#}; <ab>vgl.</ab> to this {#aBiniDAna#}\n<ls>ṚV. PRĀT. 6,5.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">9.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">11.</ls> <ls n=\"ṚV. PRĀT. 6,\">12.</ls>"}
{"key1": "DA", "subcard": "_d_a~~h0_54_upani", "iast": "upanidhā", "h": "upanidhā", "sense_tag": "1", "ru": "<div n=\"p\">— {#upani#}\n<div n=\"1\"> 1) {%ставить рядом, помещать рядом%}: {#vedO pariDIMSca SakalAMScopanidaDati#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 2,5,3,5.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">3,7,1,3.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,7,\">2,1.</ls>\n<ls>PAÑCAV. BR. 21,2,9.</ls> {#nava SarAve SamIparRAni copanihitAni Bavanti#}\n<ls>ĀŚV. GṚHY. 1,7.</ls> <ab>med.</ab>: {#daRqam#}\n<ls>GOBH. 4,9,11.</ls> {%подносить кому-л.%} (кушанье <ab>u. s. w.</ab>): {#yaTA\\nyasmA^ upAna\\DAya^ . a\\nyasmE^ pra\\yacCa^ti#} {%как если бы он одному подносил, другому действительно давал%}\n<ls>TBR. 2,1,3,6.</ls> {#yaTA yasmA aSanamAharettasmA AhftyEvopanidaDyAdevaM tat#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 2,3,1,17.</ls> {#neto 'nye (kulmAzAH) vidyante yacca ye ma ima upanihitAH#}\n<ls>CHĀND. UP. 1,10,2.</ls> <ab>med.</ab> <ls>LĀṬY. 4,11,17.</ls> {%приближать%}: {#karRayorupaniDAya#} (уста) {#meDA jananaM japati#}\n<ls>ĀŚV. GṚHY. 1,15</ls> (<ab>vgl.</ab> {#aBini#}). {%приводить, доставлять%}: {#vahati malayasamIre madanamupaniDAya#}\n<ls>GĪT. 5,2.</ls>", "de": "<div n=\"p\">— {#upani#}\n<div n=\"1\"> 1) {%daneben setzen, — stellen%}: {#vedO pariDIMSca SakalAMScopanidaDati#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 2,5,3,5.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">3,7,1,3.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,7,\">2,1.</ls>\n<ls>PAÑCAV. BR. 21,2,9.</ls> {#nava SarAve SamIparRAni copanihitAni Bavanti#}\n<ls>ĀŚV. GṚHY. 1,7.</ls> <ab>med.</ab>: {#daRqam#}\n<ls>GOBH. 4,9,11.</ls> {%Jmd%} (eine Speise <ab>u. s. w.</ab>) {%vorsetzen%}: {#yaTA\\nyasmA^ upAna\\DAya^ . a\\nyasmE^ pra\\yacCa^ti#} {%wie wenn er dem Einen vorsetzt, dem Andern wirklich giebt%}\n<ls>TBR. 2,1,3,6.</ls> {#yaTA yasmA aSanamAharettasmA AhftyEvopanidaDyAdevaM tat#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 2,3,1,17.</ls> {#neto 'nye (kulmAzAH) vidyante yacca ye ma ima upanihitAH#}\n<ls>CHĀND. UP. 1,10,2.</ls> <ab>med.</ab> <ls>LĀṬY. 4,11,17.</ls> {%nähern%}: {#karRayorupaniDAya#} (seinen Mund) {#meDA jananaM japati#}\n<ls>ĀŚV. GṚHY. 1,15</ls> (<ab>vgl.</ab> {#aBini#}). {%herbeiführen, herbeibringen%}: {#vahati malayasamIre madanamupaniDAya#}\n<ls>GĪT. 5,2.</ls>", "equivalence_type": "equivalent", "source_type": "attested", "stratum": "", "differentia": "Значение приближения к чему-л./кому-л., поднесения; upa- указывает на движение вплотную.", "review_status": "ai_translated", "reviewer": null, "provenance": {"model": "sonnet", "generator": "gen_opt_harness2.batched-masked", "schema_version": "pwg_ru.workflow_meta.v1", "root": "DA", "safe_root": "_d_a", "rootmap_sha256": "29ac182af41e4be8254a0a137fc08a355153b793cba4e1fdd80ef35b423f90fd", "input_raw_sha256": "8901f09021ac7ff07af24b1bdec54e379953a4257020b7482caeea3f0269db4b", "input_portrait_sha256": "cd1dc64925ab910b5c3b80fe126170282a60ae6de6734b008b33f2f97a8fb319", "generated_at": "2026-06-29T12:31:01Z", "wf_file": "wf_output_da_a.json", "promoted_by": "promote_final_cards.py"}, "dcs_freq": {"band": 3, "count": 51, "hapax": false, "attested": true, "core80": false, "matched": "compound", "matched_key": "upanidhā", "pos": {"counts": {"VERB": 51}, "shares": {"VERB": 1.0}, "band": {"VERB": 5}, "dominant": "VERB", "dominant_share": 1.0, "total": 51}, "genre": {"counts": {"sastra": 2, "sutra": 24, "smrti": 3, "epic": 1, "kavya": 1, "upanisad": 1, "brahmana": 14, "yajus": 2}, "band": {"sastra": 3, "sutra": 5, "smrti": 4, "epic": 2, "kavya": 3, "upanisad": 2, "brahmana": 5, "yajus": 3}}, "era": {"counts": {"Classical": 3, "Sutra-Sastra": 24, "Epic-Purana": 4, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 15, "Vedic": 2}, "band": {"Classical": 4, "Sutra-Sastra": 5, "Epic-Purana": 4, "Brahmana-Upanisad": 5, "Vedic": 3}}}, "en": "<div n=\"p\">— {#upani#}\n<div n=\"1\"> 1) to place beside, to set beside: {#vedO pariDIMSca SakalAMScopanidaDati#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 2,5,3,5.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR.\">3,7,1,3.</ls> <ls n=\"ŚAT. BR. 3,7,\">2,1.</ls>\n<ls>PAÑCAV. BR. 21,2,9.</ls> {#nava SarAve SamIparRAni copanihitAni Bavanti#}\n<ls>ĀŚV. GṚHY. 1,7.</ls> <ab>med.</ab>: {#daRqam#}\n<ls>GOBH. 4,9,11.</ls> to set before someone (a dish <ab>u. s. w.</ab>): {#yaTA\\nyasmA^ upAna\\DAya^ . a\\nyasmE^ pra\\yacCa^ti#} as when he sets before the one and actually gives to the other\n<ls>TBR. 2,1,3,6.</ls> {#yaTA yasmA aSanamAharettasmA AhftyEvopanidaDyAdevaM tat#}\n<ls>ŚAT. BR. 2,3,1,17.</ls> {#neto 'nye (kulmAzAH) vidyante yacca ye ma ima upanihitAH#}\n<ls>CHĀND. UP. 1,10,2.</ls> <ab>med.</ab> <ls>LĀṬY. 4,11,17.</ls> to bring near: {#karRayorupaniDAya#} (his mouth) {#meDA jananaM japati#}\n<ls>ĀŚV. GṚHY. 1,15</ls> (<ab>vgl.</ab> {#aBini#}). to bring about, to bring near: {#vahati malayasamIre madanamupaniDAya#}\n<ls>GĪT. 5,2.</ls>"}
